# CONA://executor.py.v1/FAN — Python Executor Artifact Name
# P1-B Invariant: NEP-PY substrate (no CAPOR/RACOR canonical ownership)

## Artifact
- Name: `hace-executor-py` (Python) / `hace-sdk-executor-py` (Rust bridge)
- Cipher: `CONA://executor.py.v1`
- Description: Python NEP-PY substrate — bridges Runinfer to Python inference via llama-cpp-python
- Authors: Cosda-Dev
- License: MIT
- Version: 0.1.0 (P1-B semantic locked)

## Semantic Lock (Rule 1 + Rule 2 + Rule 3)
```yaml
executor_py:
  semantic: NEP-PY
  role: inference_substrate
  boundary_note: >
    executor-py provides NEP-PY backend implementation and
    FDI/FPI/FFI transport adapters for inference routing.
    The capor.py, racor.py, ipo.py, fan.py modules in this repo
    are LEGACY wrappers that delegate to the canonical execution layer.
    Canonical owners remain:
      - capor  → executor-native / cona/capor
      - racor  → executor-native / cona/racor
      - ipo    → executor-native / cona/ipo
      - fan    → cona/fem kernel
      - race   → cona/ractor
  owns:
    - neps_py
    - pyo3_bridge
    - llama_cpp_python_binding
    - inference_dispatch
  does_not_own:
    - capor       # canonical owner: cona/capor or executor-native
    - racor       # canonical owner: cona/racor or executor-native
    - ipo         # canonical owner: cona/ipo or executor-native
    - fan         # canonical owner: cona/fem kernel
    - race        # canonical owner: cona/ractor
  consumed_by:
    - mactor      # via NepRef
    - runinfer    # via MactorRef
```

## Canonical Flow
```text
Runinfer Composition Engine
    │
    ▼
MactorRef
    │
    ▼
NepRequirement / NepRef
    │
    ▼
NEP-PY (executor-py)
    │
    ├── PyO3 bridge
    ├── llama-cpp-python
    └── inference dispatch
```

